  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1253 PM CDT Sat Jul 11 2026\n\nThe persistent, strong ridge aloft will be the dominant factor in \nthe region's weather through mid week. High pressure at the surface \nwill be a bit more transient, or at least not centered directly over \nthe forecast area. For ambient weather, this means hot, breezy, and \nno precip through Wednesday. The heat headlines remain unchanged \nwith highs and/or \"feels-like\" temps near or over 100 degrees \npotentially through Friday, especially around the Missouri River \ncounties. In fact, Pierre and Mobridge are forecast to be within 3 \ndegrees of record highs Sunday through Tuesday. The southerly \nbreezes will moderate the apparent temperatures during peak heating \na bit. However, gusts of 20 to 35 mph combined with the heat will \nalso quickly dry out grasses. Can't rule out needing a fire weather \nheadline by Monday when min RH falls into the upper teens west \nriver. Still a little early for a watch, but will be something to \nconsider for future forecast shifts. \n\nOvernight lows will not offer much recovery from the heat, either, \nremaining in the 70 to 75 degree range across most of the forecast \narea.",
